title: move, edit and delete steal other agents' live claims
updated: 2026-08-10T01:28:12Z
---

Found independently by two lanes. `move`, `edit` and `delete` never check who
holds a claim, so any agent can take over another agent's in-flight work:

    karr move 1 in-progress --claim alice
    karr move 1 review --claim mallory   -> rc=0, claim reassigned to mallory
    karr edit 1 -a "mallory was here"    -> rc=0
    karr delete 1 --yes                  -> rc=0

`handoff` does it correctly (`Cmd/Handoff.pm:49-54` -> "Task 1 is claimed by
mallory", rc=1) and `pick` filters claimed tasks, because `Role::ClaimTimeout`
is composed only into those two.

kanban-md calls `checkClaim` in move (`cmd/move.go:142`), edit
(`cmd/edit.go:149`), delete (`cmd/delete.go:78,129`) and handoff; `CheckClaim`
(`internal/task/validate.go:126`) allows the same claimant and expired claims.

Four commands with four different claim policies today. Fix: one shared check,
composed everywhere a task is mutated, with the same expiry semantics.
Scope note from the #86 work: handoff writes claims the same unguarded
last-writer-wins way move/edit/delete do, so it belongs in this ticket even
though the title does not name it.

Also relevant, and the reason #86 needed a card-level fix rather than a lock
fix: App::karr::Lock identifies the holder by git_user_email, so every agent
in one clone shares a lock identity. acquire() then legitimately succeeds for
all of them via the re-entrancy path -- the holder is "the same agent" as far
as the lock can tell. The ref-level exclusivity from #46 is real, but it does
not give per-agent exclusivity for anything that identifies holders that way.
Whatever guard this ticket puts on claims must key on the agent name the user
passed (--claim), not on the git identity.
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
Closed on its stated scope: move, edit and delete no longer take over a live
claim, and for move and edit the check and the write are one compare-and-swap.

The two write paths found while fixing it -- archive (no claim check at all) and
handoff (its own private copy of the rule, still read-then-write) -- are split
out as #97 rather than left as an invisible remainder on a closed ticket.
